#. fr: crapauds de mer
#. column 0: seafaring toad
#. column 8: The first sailors to spy one of these odd creatures at sea thought they had taken leave of their senses, or at the very least, had taken a wrong turn and somehow ended up in a pond.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on small canvases.]
#. column 9: Seafaring Toad
msgctxt "Item:32094:0:2"
msgid "seafaring toads"
msgstr "морские жабы"

#. ja: 河川に棲息するはずの黄緑色の両生類<br>緋汐海沖合の伝説魚<br>[魚拓額縁G1に設定可能]
#. de: Diesem Frosch einen winzigen Kapitänshut zu besorgen ist die einzig richtige Entscheidung. (Kann als Fischdruck in Rahmen der Größe S ausgestellt werden.)
#. fr: Un crapaud verdâtre, tout ce qu'il y a de plus commun, si ce n'est qu'il vit dans la mer.<br>Proie légendaire du large de la mer Pourpre.<br>[Affichable dans un cadre à ichtyogramme de petite taille]
#. column 0: seafaring toad
#. column 2: seafaring toads
#. column 9: Seafaring Toad
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "Item:32094:0:8"
msgid "The first sailors to spy one of these odd creatures at sea thought they had taken leave of their senses, or at the very least, had taken a wrong turn and somehow ended up in a pond.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on small canvases.]"
msgstr "Первые моряки, увидевшие этих странных созданий в море, решили, что лишились рассудка. Или, на худой конец, сбились с пути и каким-то образом оказались в пруду.<br><br>[Можно поместить в малую раму для ихтиограммы.]"

